  "server": [
    {
      "seq": 33,
      "files": [
        "App.gs",
        "Code.gs",
        "Hub.gs",
        "ComputingCode.gs"
      ],
      "notes": [
        "Students sign in with their name and a password (Science or Computing, chosen on the card). Old 4-number PINs still work once, then the page asks for a proper password",
        "The Teacher Hub signs in with a username and password. The first time, the Hub asks for your teacher PIN to set them. Change them in the T menu, Username and password",
        "The portal: a roomier card, a small teacher link, and stars and galaxies bent by the black hole's gravity behind NASA's simulation",
        "The decks' own sign-in box takes a password",
        "Includes release 29 (Streak Challenge). Paste: App.gs, Code.gs, Hub.gs and ComputingCode.gs, then deploy a new version. The pages update themselves"
      ]
    },
    {
      "seq": 29,
      "files": [
        "App.gs",
        "Code.gs"
      ],
      "notes": [
        "Streak Challenge (release 29): on the chapter check slide, the projector runs the check as a class game, one question at a time. Speed gives nothing: a right answer is worth 100, each right answer in a row adds 50 more (up to 300 a question), and a wrong answer ends the streak",
        "The projector shows how many have answered, then the answer, the class's choices, the top 5 and the longest streaks. Each iPad shows only the student's own result and place",
        "At the end each score becomes Worksheet Hub points: the full score earns the Chapter check points in Settings (30), a lower score its share, once per lesson. The game counts as the student's chapter check",
        "The chapter check done alone is scored the same way, so the pass mark is no longer used",
        "Paste: Code.gs and App.gs. The lesson slides update themselves"
      ]
    },
    {
      "seq": 28,
      "files": [
        "App.gs",
        "ComputingCode.gs"
      ],
